{"title":"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of all point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> in the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Coordinate_plane\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Coordinate plane\">coordinate plane</a> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/1/3b1cbc72f1dfb1393826f9228576d89bbc365f6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le x \\le \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"81\" height=\"33\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/e/56efd0c8a0248bf37fbf3c9810a7a827fbd626d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le y \\le \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"80\" height=\"33\" />.  What is the area of the subset of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/f/dbfe47d3cebb8cec2ec7292989a766db924380a7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin^2x-\\sin x \\sin y + \\sin^2y \\le \\frac34?\\]\" width=\"248\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/2/5a2abb4f0c8241dbaedb73e7a48b1c543d761d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ \\dfrac{\\pi^2}{9} \\qquad \\mathrm{(B)}\\ \\dfrac{\\pi^2}{8} \\qquad \\mathrm{(C)}\\ \\dfrac{\\pi^2}{6} \\qquad \\mathrm{(D)}\\ \\dfrac{3\\pi^2}{16} \\qquad \\mathrm{(E)}\\ \\dfrac{2\\pi^2}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"426\" height=\"39\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We start out by solving the equality first.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/e/90e429c50ff7d2d430f4f360e6277084f9ab5873.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sin^2x - \\sin x \\sin y + \\sin^2y &amp;= \\frac34 \\\\ \\sin x &amp;= \\frac{\\sin y \\pm \\sqrt{\\sin^2 y - 4 ( \\sin^2y - \\frac34 ) }}{2} \\\\  &amp;= \\frac{\\sin y \\pm \\sqrt{3 - 3 \\sin^2 y }}{2} \\\\  &amp;= \\frac{\\sin y \\pm \\sqrt{3 \\cos^2 y }}{2} \\\\  &amp;= \\frac12 \\sin y \\pm \\frac{\\sqrt3}{2} \\cos y \\\\ \\sin x &amp;= \\sin (y \\pm \\frac{\\pi}{3}) \\end{align*}\" width=\"468\" height=\"279\" />\nWe end up with three lines that matter: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/a/d4a4f05367391c0d8b7012af2c77f31349a0de52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = y + \\frac\\pi3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"80\" height=\"33\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e5747262239b6bd63701c90e7da1378d12d3ccbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = y - \\frac\\pi3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"80\" height=\"33\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/8/d48708f4172a69288665d680735d6e6545ec1483.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\pi - (y + \\frac\\pi3) = \\frac{2\\pi}{3} - y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"208\" height=\"37\" />.  We plot these lines below.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/2/0b260cfae48ccfba4d3965e319cf0157f545541d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(5cm); D((0,0)--(3,0)--(3,3)--(0,3)--cycle); D((1,-0.1)--(1,0.1)); D((2,-0.1)--(2,0.1)); D((-0.1,1)--(0.1,1)); D((-0.1,2)--(0.1,2)); D((2,0)--(3,1)--(1,3)--(0,2)); MP(&quot;\\frac{\\pi}{6}&quot;, (1,0), plain.S); MP(&quot;\\frac{\\pi}{3}&quot;, (2,0), plain.S); MP(&quot;\\frac{\\pi}{2}&quot;, (3,0), plain.S); MP(&quot;\\frac{\\pi}{6}&quot;, (0,1), plain.W); MP(&quot;\\frac{\\pi}{3}&quot;, (0,2), plain.W); MP(&quot;\\frac{\\pi}{2}&quot;, (0,3), plain.W); [/asy]\" width=\"228\" height=\"238\" />\nNote that by testing the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/f/7df738db118b72498bdc1115bf57649acb94e932.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\pi/6,\\pi/6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />, we can see that we want the area of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pentagon\" title=\"Pentagon\">pentagon</a>.  We can calculate that by calculating the area of the square and then subtracting the area of the 3 triangles. (Note we could also do this by adding the areas of the isosceles triangle in the bottom left corner and the rectangle with the previous triangle's hypotenuse as the longer side.)\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/6/9960974f3e746e6c6a8f09944e77b21d0bb7d877.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} A &amp;= \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)^2 - 2 \\cdot \\frac12 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)^2 - \\frac12 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)^2 \\\\ &amp;= \\pi^2 \\left ( \\frac14 - \\frac1{36} - \\frac1{18}\\right ) \\\\ &amp;= \\pi^2 \\left ( \\frac{9-1-2}{36} \\right ) = \\boxed{\\text{(C)}\\ \\frac{\\pi^2}{6}} \\end{align*}\" width=\"286\" height=\"143\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can write the given equation as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/2/2725e0e8e00d3e8fb9e55ba36990d56b95d62e75.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin^3x + \\sin^3y \\le \\frac{3}{4}(\\sin x + \\sin y).\\]\" width=\"255\" height=\"37\" /> Note that when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d348bde3e15456e71734dc2c56fc7425c95927f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/8/06831c9585762a83a9bca2dcc3c802d9d8379523.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin y \\le \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"43\" /> which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/5/2051f91d701f0870ea9778aade3dacb5af2517fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\le \\frac{\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"51\" height=\"34\" />. Similary we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/e/36e0c50b9f10fba2c65d38f55b6d1c97d8c666bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\le \\frac{\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"51\" height=\"34\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a06334068417b1781d14e8b28af827907961eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />. Then we see what happens at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/4/d04f02535ba0d4d2e88dd26b9ce36c7a24cd7057.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"48\" height=\"33\" />. Clearly at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/4/d04f02535ba0d4d2e88dd26b9ce36c7a24cd7057.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"48\" height=\"33\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/e/95e474f06f50ff7556c969506eaf6702943934a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\le \\frac{\\pi}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"51\" height=\"34\" />. By symmetry we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/f/73f70e90a005447dcda477ff61799bd9a211c68e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\le \\frac{\\pi}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"51\" height=\"34\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/0/5e0f63cc83c328a50cc2c1cc9335d34bf05b8e3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"51\" height=\"34\" />. So we get a graph like \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/2/0b260cfae48ccfba4d3965e319cf0157f545541d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(5cm); D((0,0)--(3,0)--(3,3)--(0,3)--cycle); D((1,-0.1)--(1,0.1)); D((2,-0.1)--(2,0.1)); D((-0.1,1)--(0.1,1)); D((-0.1,2)--(0.1,2)); D((2,0)--(3,1)--(1,3)--(0,2)); MP(&quot;\\frac{\\pi}{6}&quot;, (1,0), plain.S); MP(&quot;\\frac{\\pi}{3}&quot;, (2,0), plain.S); MP(&quot;\\frac{\\pi}{2}&quot;, (3,0), plain.S); MP(&quot;\\frac{\\pi}{6}&quot;, (0,1), plain.W); MP(&quot;\\frac{\\pi}{3}&quot;, (0,2), plain.W); MP(&quot;\\frac{\\pi}{2}&quot;, (0,3), plain.W); [/asy]\" width=\"228\" height=\"238\" />\nThus the area of what we are interested in is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/9/c1914a5b3b2289b34efa941949bce0d35066230a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\pi^2}{4} - (\\frac{\\pi^2}{18} + \\frac{\\pi^2}{36}) = \\frac{\\pi^2}{6}.\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"39\" />\n~coolmath_2018\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B\">2006 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/